    "more": "Some things are settled by courts and tribunals: the Holocaust, the genocide in Rwanda, and the genocide at Srebrenica. Others are widely recognized, such as the Armenian genocide. On Israel and Palestine, the International Court of Justice found in July 2024 that Israel's continued presence in the occupied Palestinian territory is unlawful and must end. Human Rights Watch, Amnesty International and the Israeli group B'Tselem have each concluded that Israeli authorities are committing the crime of apartheid against Palestinians. An independent United Nations commission, Amnesty International and Israeli human rights organizations have concluded that Israel has committed genocide in Gaza. The International Court of Justice has not yet ruled on that question, and the case will take years. Saying who found what is not hedging. It lets a reader check, and it keeps a true statement from being dismissed because it claimed too much.",
