    "body": "Phrases like wipe them out, send them all back, drive them into the sea, or clear them out ask for a whole people to be removed. Each time it has been tried, it has meant killing, expulsion and ruin, to many peoples in many places. The wish often grows from real pain, fear or loss. The need underneath, such as safety, home, dignity or justice, can be met in ways that do not require anyone to disappear.",
    "tryIt": "If you notice the thought all of them, or get rid of them, try finishing the sentence: what I most need is. Then ask whether that need could be met without anyone being removed.",
