    "key": "Anger at those who took land or rule is understandable, and words that make them less than human still do harm.",
    "body": "People whose land, home or freedom was taken have real grief and rage, and nobody here tells them to feel otherwise. The anger points at something real: a system, a policy, an army, a set of laws. Calling everyone in a category vermin, or asking for them all to disappear, folds individuals into the system and invites the same violence back. It also leaves the original need, such as land, safety, dignity or return, untouched.",
    "tryIt": "Try naming what was taken from you or your people, and what you most want now. Then notice whether that wish is about a system changing or about people ceasing to exist.",
