    "contentNote": "",
    "key": "A belief is a thought, and how much it hurts to question it does not decide whether it is true.",
    "body": "Faith can hold what matters most to a person: belonging, meaning, comfort, safety. When a belief is questioned, the hurt is real and worth listening to. A belief is also a thought, and thoughts can be looked at: what does it claim, what does it ask of people, and what is it protecting? Hearing the need under the hurt does not mean agreeing, and examining a claim is not an attack on the person.",
    "tryIt": "Think of a belief you hold dear. What does it give you? Then ask what you would want from someone who disagreed with it.",
