    "more": "The same process runs for every thought, a religious one included. We listen for the feeling and the need under it, such as respect, belonging, safety or meaning. We can also ask what happened and what the belief says. A feeling can be fully honored while a claim is still examined. What is not accepted is hurt used as a reason that nothing can be said, or a belief used to justify harming or removing a people. Saying that something offends a faith opens the same conversation as saying it offends me: what is the hurt, and what is the need?",
