    "key": "What a survivor of violence feels is theirs to feel, and nobody is asked to feel differently.",
    "body": "After violence, rage, grief, fear and mistrust make sense. They are not a flaw, and they are not the survivor's fault. Listening to the anger is not agreeing with a plan to harm others. Underneath there is often a need for safety, justice, being believed or someone to be accountable. Those needs matter, and they can be met without anyone being made less than human.",
